{"name":"Little Red Corvette","hex":"#e50102","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"little","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Small, not large, limited, particularly:","Small, limited in size."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Not much.","Not at all."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/little"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"corvette","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flush-decked warship of the 17th-18th centuries having a single tier of guns; it ranked next below a frigate; called in the United States navy a sloop-of-war.","In a modern navy, a lightly armed and armoured blue water warship, smaller than a frigate, capable of transoceanic duty.\n A starship of comparable role"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corvette"}],"entries":[{"title":"Little Red Corvette","blocks":[{"text":"\"Little Red Corvette\" is a song by American recording artist Prince. The song combines a Linn LM-1 beat and slow synth buildup with a rock chorus, over which Prince, using several automobile metaphors, recalls a one-night stand with a beautiful promiscuous woman. Backing vocals were performed by Lisa Coleman and Dez Dickerson; Dickerson also performs a guitar solo on the song."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/15/Prince_LRC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Red_Corvette","wikidata":"Q2342791"},{"title":"Corvette","blocks":[{"text":"A corvette is a small warship. It is traditionally the smallest class of vessel considered to be rated a warship. The warship class above the corvette is that of the frigate, while the class below was historically that of the sloop-of-war."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Zarechny_%28parade%29.jpg/330px-Zarechny_%28parade%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corvette","wikidata":"Q170013"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/80-G-289820_HMCS_Riviere_du_Loup_%28K_357%29.jpg/500px-80-G-289820_HMCS_Riviere_du_Loup_%28K_357%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/80-G-289820_HMCS_Riviere_du_Loup_%28K_357%29.jpg/1280px-80-G-289820_HMCS_Riviere_du_Loup_%28K_357%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/80-G-289820_HMCS_Riviere_du_Loup_%28K_357%29.jpg/500px-80-G-289820_HMCS_Riviere_du_Loup_%2